  "title": "Dick\u2019s Sporting Goods (DKS): Comparing today\u2019s promotional environment to 2017",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-09-28",
  "insights": [
   "The current promotional environment in sporting goods is driven by excess inventory in legacy footwear silhouettes, contrasting with 2017 when pressures were broader across athletic apparel and hunting.",
   "Dick's Sporting Goods is better positioned today than in 2017 due to stronger vendor relationships (including Nike), a significant private label business (~13% of sales), and the 'Going, Going Gone!' clearance banner.",
   "JD Sports reported soft footwear performance in North America due to consumer pressures and product cycle transitions, though apparel and accessories remain solid.",
   "Foot Locker's EMEA business is facing aggressive promotional pressure and cautious consumer sentiment, with management expecting these dynamics to persist through 4Q26.",
   "Academy Sports & Outdoors is largely insulated from the current lifestyle footwear slowdown due to a more diverse assortment, including outdoor, work boots, and performance running.",
   "The 2017 promotional cycle was triggered by major industry bankruptcies (Sports Authority, Sport Chalet, Golfsmith) and aggressive DTC shifts, with inventory largely cleared by 1Q18.",
   "Dick's management believes the narrative that the athletic cycle is over is 'overdone' and notes the company can pivot to alternative categories, unlike specialty retailers more dependent on launch product."
